Modifications
-------------
  Modified by Yansunsky, beginning July 2026 and continuing to the present.
  Forked from the upstream branch dev/NeoForge-1.21.1 at commit e3ea859.

  This version is released under the GNU Affero General Public License,
  version 3, the same license as the upstream work. See LICENSE in this
  directory for the full license text.

  Corresponding source code:
  https://github.com/yansunsky/Sweeper-Maid

  Summary of changes (full details in the project README):
    - Dustbin paging: the bottom row of the chest holds server-synthesized
      paging buttons, so players without the mod can page too. 45 content
      slots per page instead of 54; existing worlds are re-packed on load.
    - Configurable per-slot stack capacity (DUSTBIN_SLOT_CAPACITY, default
      1,000,000) replacing the vanilla limit of 64.
    - Swept experience orbs are converted into retrievable items
      (experience bottles, or Create experience nuggets when Create is
      loaded) instead of being destroyed.
    - Scheduled dustbin upkeep: clear, or pack to a gzipped NBT file that
      can be imported again.
    - Global re-sort of dustbin contents after each sweep.
    - Experience orbs are now counted by the overload threshold.
    - The dustbin is served over a vanilla chest menu, so unmodded clients
      are no longer disconnected during the handshake.

